 "text": "Hi, how are you doing? Six is a good age to introduce real food. Oatmeal biscuits, greek yogurt, soft cheese cut into cubes, and cooked chicken are all fine. Six year olds are big kids, and they like to try new things. You can mix the yellow food with the new stuff and she' likely like it. Coffee is fine at any age, just keep it black and only small amounts first. Sure. Let her pour the yogurt, mix the risotto, or even crack the eggs. It' a great way to teach her about food and make the week feel less like a visit.",
